# shell: desktop
# CW-042: Select… names a window, and named it without opening one.  The
# single-window shell has no Select window to open, so this half is the
# multi-window shell's.
wait 6
press 300 300 3
wait 2
release 300 300 3
wait 5
menu-pick Select…
wait 8
expect-title Select
note its foot is where a 12 px face puts it
note the backdrop below its foot, in the front window's shadow
expect-pixel 400 372 234669
key w ctrl
wait 6
note now raise the interface to 16 px and ask for this window again:
note its rows and its height were written down for a 12 px face, so this
note is the only size at which a wrong number would show
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Fonts
wait 12
expect-title Fonts
key Tab
key Tab
key Return
wait 12
key Return
wait 12
expect-font Sans 16
key w ctrl
wait 8
press 300 300 3
wait 2
release 300 300 3
wait 5
menu-pick Select…
wait 10
expect-title Select
note and now its two fields and its tick row are each a line of text
note taller, so the window is twenty pixels deeper
expect-pixel 400 372 d8d8d8
quit
